WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Morai Rabotai, ladies and gentlemen.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:29.000
The purpose of this paper is to develop a kind of theory in which we could understand the role of qabbala as a factor in apostasy, in the conversion of Jews in Spain.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:35.680
In order to understand the role of qabbala as a factor in apostasy, a few

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:41.760
clarifications are of the essence. Our understanding of Judaism today, of

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:47.800
rabbinic Judaism, it's a little bit different than that of the Judaism in

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:55.760
Spain prior to the rise of qabbala. At that time, we had what we call the

00:00:55.760 --> 00:01:01.340
Maimonidesian. It is not a uniform tradition, but there are some very basic

00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:07.000
points, and those basic points later on through the rise of qabbala were

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:14.880
questioned. Point number one, in the philosophy of Maimonides, Yudah Alevi, etc.,

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:21.620
the basis of the Tora is a covenant, is a historic covenant. The historic

00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:29.620
covenant results in misva, in commandments. Now, the most important aspect is that those misva,

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:36.940
as Yehudah Levi defines them, are mazbuta. Each misva is mazbuta. Mazbuta means properly and

00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:44.820
accurately defined. So therefore, Judaism is committed not to a concept, but to a specific

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:53.060
definition of the misva. Those definitions were the patrimony not of

00:01:53.060 --> 00:02:00.400
individual scholars or individual rabbis but rather of the Bedin and it was a

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:06.500
transmission from one court to another court as my mind is in the Mishne Tora

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:14.500
explains Tora Shebe Alpeh is Masha Masar Bedin, Mipi Bedin. It is a Jewish

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:21.100
court. Now this Jewish court, it was a national, and I underline national,

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:29.060
institution of the Jews. With termination of the end of the Talmudic period, 499,

00:02:29.060 --> 00:02:37.840
according to traditional sources, we no longer had a public bed din, but we have

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:43.000
only individual bed din, shal yachidim, that's what my ma'alad says, all right?

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:53.000
Now, therefore, here comes a very important thing. Judaism, as Yehuda Halevi says, is different than all other religions.

00:02:53.000 --> 00:03:02.000
And precisely these three points. It is the result of the covenant. And because it is the result of the covenant, Yehuda Halevi says,

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:09.920
ishtihad which means personal endeavor conjecture ideas whether it comes from the heart or from the

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:17.440
mind according to judah levy into the whole school yes it is not part of the jewish religion says

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:22.960
according it says otherwise says if you would accept ishtihad as a source for religion then

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:29.360
you cannot distinguish between judaism those who believe in polytheism sources witchcraft and all

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:35.440
kind of intellectual and spiritual aberrations. So point number one is, therefore, Judaism,

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:44.040
it is not and cannot accept ijtihad as a source of spirituality. Number two, very important,

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:51.120
whatever it is based upon ijtihad, therefore, it is abodazara. Abodazara in the sense that

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:57.720
it is idolatry, not as Christianity interprets idolatry, and later on Jews interpret idolatry,

00:03:57.720 --> 00:04:02.520
not as worshipping of idols, but as avodah shehizarah,

00:04:03.140 --> 00:04:08.500
a law or a kind of service to God which is not prescribed by the law.

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:12.780
And therefore, according to Judah Alevi, as he pointed very clearly,

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:17.520
it says the Jews were permitted to worship the kerubim at the temple,

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:21.600
although there were images, because that was part of what the law prescribed.

00:04:22.480 --> 00:04:26.000
So the difference between 'Aboda Zara and non-'Aboda Zara

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:29.440
is precisely on the matter of ijtihad.

00:04:29.980 --> 00:04:31.680
Because we do not accept ijtihad,

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:40.120
and therefore we do not accept religion as based upon personal opinion,

