00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:29.080
we no longer have a Bedin, and therefore we cannot be possibly a nation.

00:06:29.260 --> 00:06:35.120
Now, since we do not have a Bedin, then we can understand another point of the Ramban.

00:06:35.780 --> 00:06:39.920
The rabbis had no right to legislate from the Tora.

00:06:40.740 --> 00:06:45.140
The Tora has not given the rabbis the right to legislate.

00:06:45.140 --> 00:06:51.260
This is a focal point, this dispute between Ramban and the Rambam.

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:56.300
According to the Rambam, all the rabbinic legislation has its basis in the Tora.

00:06:56.720 --> 00:06:58.700
Lot asumi adavar she'agiyuech hayamin usmol.

00:06:59.120 --> 00:07:03.200
But according to the Ramban, it says very clearly, legislation is no longer the oraita.

00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:10.780
We have no obligation from the Tora to obey or to listen or to comply with the rabbinic legislation.

00:07:10.780 --> 00:07:16.300
So therefore, what is the source of rabbinic authority?

00:07:16.740 --> 00:07:18.080
Here comes something very interesting.

00:07:18.680 --> 00:07:22.620
It is not, obviously, a national institution,

00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:25.280
like the Jews believed for generations,

00:07:25.480 --> 00:07:27.520
from the time of the Geonim, etc.,

00:07:27.520 --> 00:07:31.440
