00:08:16.580 --> 00:08:23.120
the method of eminionics of the rabbis is what I call that of the Stoics.

00:08:23.780 --> 00:08:26.140
By that of the Stoics, it means we make connections.

00:08:26.300 --> 00:08:30.720
We take one term here and one term another one, and we connect these two terms.

00:08:30.880 --> 00:08:36.220
And out of connecting these two terms, we generate, yes, some sort of an idea.

00:08:36.220 --> 00:08:37.460
Let me give you a simple example.

00:08:37.920 --> 00:08:40.560
We have the word le'avdo, to serve God.

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:45.340
Now, always to serve God in the Pentateuch means through sacrifice,

00:08:45.520 --> 00:08:46.800
through sacramental sacrifice.

00:08:47.240 --> 00:08:49.680
And then we have le'avchem, heart.

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:51.760
And then we connect these two terms.

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:52.100
It says,

00:08:52.420 --> 00:08:59.360
And then we invent or we establish or we create the notion of tefilla.

00:08:59.540 --> 00:09:02.400
It is by connecting two different terms,

00:09:03.200 --> 00:09:04.600
exactly like the Stoics did it,

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:09.360
that we generate a third idea, A, and B produces C.

00:09:09.980 --> 00:09:11.840
Now, because of this,

00:09:12.340 --> 00:09:16.680
and now you're going to understand another crucial point of Rambam and Ramban controversy.

